From: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 20:53:22 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath11k: handle country channel restrictions

QCN9074 firmware can advertise 160 MHz for the CN 5735-5835 MHz
rule. cfg80211 rejects the entire regulatory domain because the
bandwidth exceeds the frequency range. Bound bandwidth to that range
without changing frequencies, power, PSD or flags. AUTO_BW continues
to determine the supported channel widths from adjacent rules.

A 6 GHz-only radio can have no usable channels in the selected country.
Skip the empty firmware channel-list update instead of raising a
kernel warning. Keep all cfg80211 channel restrictions in effect.

Signed-off-by: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/reg.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/reg.c
@@ -145,8 +145,14 @@
 		}
 	}
 
-	if (WARN_ON(!num_channels))
-		return -EINVAL;
+	/* A band can be unavailable in the selected country. Keep the
+	 * cfg80211 channel restrictions and wait for a usable channel list.
+	 */
+	if (!num_channels) {
+		ath11k_dbg(ar->ab, ATH11K_DBG_REG,
+			   "no usable channels for this regulatory domain\n");
+		return 0;
+	}
 
 	params = kzalloc_flex(*params, ch_param, num_channels);
 	if (!params)
@@ -397,6 +403,10 @@
 		       u32 end_freq, u32 bw, u32 ant_gain, u32 reg_pwr,
 		       s8 psd, u32 reg_flags)
 {
+	/* Firmware can advertise 160 MHz for a 100 MHz country rule. */
+	if (end_freq > start_freq)
+		bw = min_t(u32, bw, end_freq - start_freq);
+
 	reg_rule->freq_range.start_freq_khz = MHZ_TO_KHZ(start_freq);
 	reg_rule->freq_range.end_freq_khz = MHZ_TO_KHZ(end_freq);
 	reg_rule->freq_range.max_bandwidth_khz = MHZ_TO_KHZ(bw);
